{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20119",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 6.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor. They're in and comfortable, and I have the measurements ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.31,
      "end_seconds": 11.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.65,
      "end_seconds": 19.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Yeah, doctor, I'll sit in if that's okay, I know what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.63,
      "end_seconds": 24.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.25,
      "end_seconds": 30.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "I'm here because of a feeling of fullness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.32,
      "end_seconds": 33.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.65,
      "end_seconds": 41.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "I'd say about a month, um, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 43.05,
      "end_seconds": 47.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "I think it's been nearer about two months, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.51,
      "end_seconds": 56.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.65,
      "end_seconds": 58.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.38,
      "end_seconds": 63.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.57,
      "end_seconds": 69.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.2,
      "end_seconds": 78.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.65,
      "text": "So, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 78.95,
      "end_seconds": 85.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "I mean, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.68,
      "end_seconds": 90.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.57,
      "end_seconds": 96.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.04,
      "end_seconds": 115.32,
      "duration_seconds": 17.28,
      "text": "Ah, and there's sudden hearing loss in my left ear as well, about a week now. So, um, and I've been feeling a bit dizzy as well, since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.06,
      "end_seconds": 119.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.64,
      "end_seconds": 121.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Mostly mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.3,
      "end_seconds": 128.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.83,
      "end_seconds": 138.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "Mm, uh, it's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.28,
      "end_seconds": 149.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.59,
      "end_seconds": 153.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "It happens on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 154.94,
      "end_seconds": 157.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.37,
      "end_seconds": 164.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any discharge, head injury or recent flying?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.28,
      "end_seconds": 180.83,
      "duration_seconds": 14.55,
      "text": "Hmm, no, no discharge, no head injury, no recent flying. I did have a ringing in the ear at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.59,
      "end_seconds": 189.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any headache or ear pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.55,
      "end_seconds": 192.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.35,
      "end_seconds": 197.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Okay, any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.01,
      "end_seconds": 202.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.08,
      "end_seconds": 206.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.37,
      "end_seconds": 211.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, um, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.99,
      "end_seconds": 214.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.06,
      "end_seconds": 217.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.18,
      "end_seconds": 222.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Okay, which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 224.23,
      "end_seconds": 229.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Mm, she takes valsartan, once a day for my blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.32,
      "end_seconds": 233.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 234.05,
      "end_seconds": 241.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "80 milligrams. Ah, uh, it's sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.26,
      "end_seconds": 246.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Since when have you been taking it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 247.9,
      "end_seconds": 258.65,
      "duration_seconds": 10.75,
      "text": "Two months now. Hmm, she is on bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day, I give it to her."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.29,
      "end_seconds": 265.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Oh, I used to take glimepiride, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.02,
      "end_seconds": 272.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.21,
      "end_seconds": 279.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.13,
      "end_seconds": 297.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.19,
      "end_seconds": 310.66,
      "duration_seconds": 12.47,
      "text": "I, I have high blood pressure. I've never really been one for hospitals. I have diabetes. Yes, an irregular heartbeat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.0,
      "end_seconds": 325.92,
      "duration_seconds": 13.92,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Right, so high blood pressure and an irregular heartbeat are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.78,
      "end_seconds": 331.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.27,
      "end_seconds": 335.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.12,
      "end_seconds": 339.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 353.52,
      "end_seconds": 362.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Heart rate 77, temperature 36.8. Saturation 98 percent, blood pressure 122 over 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.94,
      "end_seconds": 363.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Right, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.15,
      "end_seconds": 370.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.88,
      "end_seconds": 374.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.89,
      "end_seconds": 391.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Both eardrums look normal and a tuning fork is heard better in the right ear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 397.06,
      "end_seconds": 426.51,
      "duration_seconds": 29.45,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Okay, thinking it through, I think we're dealing with sudden loss of hearing that needs urgent assessment at this stage. It could also be a middle ear fluid problem, so we'll keep that open. Wax is still possible. Let's get a hearing test, for sudden hearing loss. Let's get an MRI scan, for unilateral hearing loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.8,
      "end_seconds": 449.82,
      "duration_seconds": 22.02,
      "text": "For this, prednisolone, 60 milligrams, once a day in the morning, for seven days. That should help with sudden hearing loss. Please attend the hearing test today if you can, as timing matters. Let's get you seen by the ear specialists, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 451.33,
      "end_seconds": 454.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Alright, you know, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.27,
      "end_seconds": 459.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Come back in one week. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 461.5,
      "end_seconds": 466.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Good, um, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 467.97,
      "end_seconds": 469.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}